  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Ausbildungsfonds f&#xfc;r Berufsbildung und Besch&#xe4;ftigung: MFC Kamza</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Fund for Vocational Training and Employment: MFC Kamza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Die wirtschaftliche Entwicklung Albaniens leidet unter einem substantiellen Fachkr&#xe4;ftemangel. Es besteht die paradoxe Situation einer hohen (Jugend-)Arbeitslosigkeit, w&#xe4;hrend Unternehmen gleichzeitig dringend qualifizierte Arbeitskr&#xe4;fte ben&#xf6;tigen. Mit dem Projekt wird die Arbeitsmarktrelevanz der beruflichen Ausbildung und damit die Besch&#xe4;ftigungsf&#xe4;higkeit von Absolventen des Multifunctional Centres (MFC) Kamza verbessert. Die Schule hat in Albanien Vorbildcharakter im Hinblick auf arbeitsmarktrelevante Berufsausbildungsangebote und das Konzept soll landesweit ausgerollt werden.Das Projekt finanziert den Ausbau des Schulcampus, moderne Ausstattung und Beratung, um die Qualit&#xe4;t und Quantit&#xe4;t des Ausbildungsangebots am MFC Kamza zu verbessern. Empf&#xe4;nger der Mittel und Projektpartner ist das Ministerium f&#xfc;r Finanzen und Wirtschaft (MoFE).Zielgruppe sind Jugendliche und junge Erwachsene, die an MFC Kamza Ausbildungsprogrammen teilnehmen. Dar&#xfc;ber hinaus profitieren Lehrer, Trainer und F&#xfc;hrungskr&#xe4;fte des MFC Kamza von den Projektma&#xdf;nahmen. Indirekt profitiert auch der Privatsektor von der verbesserten Ausbildung durch den Zugang zu mehr Fachkr&#xe4;ften.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The economic development of Albania suffers from a substantial shortage of skilled workers. There is the paradoxical situation of high (youth) unemployment, while at the same time companies urgently need qualified workers. With the project, the labour market relevance of the vocational education and training and thus employability of graduates from the Multifunctional Centre (MFC) Kamza is improved. The school has model character in Albania with regard to labour market relevant vocational training offers, the concept is supposed to be rolled-out throughout the country.The project finances the expansion of the campus, modern equipment and technical assistance to improve the quality and quantity of the training offer at MFC Kamza. Recipient of the funds and project partner is the Ministry of Finance and Economy (MoFE). The target group comprises young people and young adults taking part in MFC training programmes. In addition, teachers, trainers and management staff at MFC Kamza will benefit from the project measures. Indirectly, the private sector also benefits from the improved training through access to an increased number of skilled workers.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Quantitative und qualitative Verbesserung der Berufsschulbildung am MFC Kamza</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The economic development of Albania suffers from a substantial shortage of skilled workers. There is the paradoxical situation of high (youth) unemployment, while at the same time companies urgently need qualified workers. With the project, the labour market relevance of the vocational education and training and thus employability of graduates from the Multifunctional Centre (MFC) Kamza is improved. The school has model character in Albania with regard to labour market relevant vocational training offers, the concept is supposed to be rolled-out throughout the country.The project finances the expansion of the campus, modern equipment and technical assistance to improve the quality and quantity of the training offer at MFC Kamza. Recipient of the funds and project partner is the Ministry of Finance and Economy (MoFE). The target group comprises young people and young adults taking part in MFC training programmes. In addition, teachers, trainers and management staff at MFC Kamza will benefit from the project measures. Indirectly, the private sector also benefits from the improved training through access to an increased number of skilled workers.</narrative>
  </description>
